sec.p:
The basic unit of combinatorial activity is a pair of TFs. Several modes of TF interaction include independence, dominance, and cooperativity 37,57–59. To mathematically define how TF pairs functionally interact in the context of transcriptional reprogramming, we used a previously established framework to model interactions by linear regression 37. Briefly, we modeled changes in gene expression observed in doubly perturbed cells (AB) as a linear combination of singly perturbed cells (A and B alone) (Figure 5A):


δAB=c0+c1δA+c2δB+ε
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{AB}=c_{0}+c_{1} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~A}+c_{2} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~B}+\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}$$\end{document}

Published studies indicate that reprogramming TFs can interact nonlinearly 25,37. To represent one type of non-linear cooperative interaction between A and B, we augmented our linear model by incorporating a cooperative component (c3δA⨯B), similar to a previous study 17 (Figure 5A, Supplemental Table 6):
δAB=c0+c1δA+c2δB+c3δA×B+ε \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{AB}=c_{0}+c_{1} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~A}+c_{2} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~B}+c_{3} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~A} \times \mathrm{B}+\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}$$\end{document}
Using this augmented linear model, we identified 46 TFs that behaved cooperatively (c3, p < 0.05), where TFs are multiplicatively cooperative (e.g., Atf3, Gata6; Figure 5G-H). To characterize other types of non-linear interactions, we also identified 79 neomorphic interactions (large mean absolute error). (e.g., Etv1 and Mlip; Figure 5G, Figure S5H).

To determine the dominant effect of TF pairs (AB), the results of linear models (1, 2, 3) were taken into consideration.
(2)
δAB=c0+c1δA+ε \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \delta \mathrm{AB}=c_{0}+c_{1} \delta \mathrm{~A}+\varepsilon \tag{2} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}

TF pairs (AB) were modeled using (4), and t-statistics of c1, c2 and c3 were calculated. If the p-value associated with the t-statistic of c3 is less than 0.05, this pair of TFs was characterized as interactive.
(4)
δAB=c0+c1δA+c2δB+c3δA×B+ε \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{AB}=c_{0}+c_{1} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~A}+c_{2} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~B}+c_{3} \boldsymbol{\delta} \mathrm{~A} \times \mathrm{B}+\boldsymbol{\varepsilon} \tag{4} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
